('18b271fd-82c2-59f9-bdb3-24b6ea70424d'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Special Senses', 'The tonotopic organization of the cochlea is preserved in the auditory cortex as:', '["No tonotopy in cortex","Columnar organization","Hierarchical layers","Circular arrangement","Random distribution"]'::jsonb, 'Columnar organization', 'Neurons with the same best frequency are organized into columns.'),
('e127ba84-e592-5859-b6e4-3ebdf17180e5'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Special Senses', 'The auditory cortex has which type of organization?', '["None","Somatotopic","Tonotopic","Retinotopic","Chemotopic"]'::jsonb, 'Tonotopic', 'The auditory cortex is organized tonotopically, with a map of sound frequency.'),
('41fff9a9-443f-5e57-aa76-abfcc1687911'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Special Senses', 'The dorsal cochlear nucleus is involved in:', '["Spectral processing and integration with somatosensory input","Temporal coding mediated physiological mechanism","Binaural localization mediated physiological mechanism","Efferent feedback mediated physiological mechanism","Simple sound detection mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Spectral processing and integration with somatosensory input', 'The dorsal cochlear nucleus processes spectral cues for sound localization.'),
