('9f747383-464a-5de5-be5f-ea16bdff3aed'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'hCG is structurally similar to:', '["FSH","Prolactin","ACTH","LH","TSH"]'::jsonb, 'LH', 'hCG and LH have a similar alpha subunit; the beta subunit of hCG is longer.'),
('ffe4fdae-4eb9-5506-9076-9cbe0d1a3949'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'Pregnancy tests detect:', '["Prolactin","Estrogen","hPL","Beta-hCG in urine or serum","Progesterone"]'::jsonb, 'Beta-hCG in urine or serum', 'Home and clinical pregnancy tests use antibodies specific to the beta subunit of hCG.'),
('0772c5b1-8239-5d8b-ba5a-dd5fc2c3bc7a'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'Placental hormones include:', '["Oxytocin mediated physiological mechanism","hCG, hPL (human placental lactogen), progesterone, estrogen, relaxin","Only progesterone mediated physiological mechanism","Prolactin mediated physiological mechanism","Only hCG mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'hCG, hPL (human placental lactogen), progesterone, estrogen, relaxin', 'The placenta is a major endocrine organ producing hormones to maintain pregnancy and prepare for lactation.'),
('1826139e-d8fd-544f-9fc2-202a11076b13'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'Human placental lactogen (hPL) is similar to:', '["Growth hormone","FSH","Prolactin","ACTH","TSH"]'::jsonb, 'Growth hormone', 'hPL has GH-like activity, promoting maternal lipolysis and insulin resistance for fetal glucose supply.'),
('5ddaedfb-76a1-56bc-a4f3-1bb32fb7ec8d'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'During pregnancy, maternal estrogen and progesterone are produced by:', '["Maternal pituitary","Maternal ovary","Corpus luteum throughout","Fetal adrenal only","Placenta"]'::jsonb, 'Placenta', 'After ~8-10 weeks, the placenta takes over hormone production from the corpus luteum.'),
('c6f69a9c-f1d7-55a5-873c-ae413517c3e6'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'The fetal-placental unit involves cooperation between:', '["Fetal liver and placenta","Fetal ovary and placenta","Fetal adrenal (produces DHEA-S) and placenta","Maternal ovary and placenta","Fetal pituitary and placenta"]'::jsonb, 'Fetal adrenal (produces DHEA-S) and placenta', 'The fetal adrenal produces DHEA-S, which the placenta aromatizes to estriol.'),
