('35a2fffd-dc0c-5513-85a7-4797294dbeab'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'Oligohydramnios (low amniotic fluid) is associated with:', '["Maternal diabetes","Multiple gestation","Fetal macrosomia","Preterm labor","Fetal renal anomalies"]'::jsonb, 'Fetal renal anomalies', 'Low amniotic fluid suggests inadequate fetal urine production.'),
('878d4290-f773-505e-8ecf-59037fc1971f'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'Polyhydramnios (excess amniotic fluid) is associated with:', '["Fetal GI obstruction (e.g., esophageal atresia), neural tube defects, maternal diabetes","Oligohydramnios mediated physiological mechanism","Fetal renal agenesis mediated physiological mechanism","Placental insufficiency mediated physiological mechanism","Structural heart disease mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Fetal GI obstruction (e.g., esophageal atresia), neural tube defects, maternal diabetes', 'Excess fluid occurs when the fetus cannot swallow or with CNS defects.'),
('960241d5-8c54-5fd5-bd5f-721458aad21c'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'The umbilical cord contains:', '["Three veins","Two arteries and two veins","One artery and one vein","Two veins and one artery","Two umbilical arteries and one umbilical vein"]'::jsonb, 'Two umbilical arteries and one umbilical vein', 'The umbilical cord has two arteries carrying deoxygenated blood to the placenta and one vein carrying oxygenated blood.'),
('56063557-a215-587b-bc68-966620370d3a'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'Reproduction', 'The ductus venosus connects:', '["Pulmonary artery to aorta","Hepatic vein to IVC","Portal vein to IVC","Umbilical vein to the inferior vena cava","Umbilical artery to aorta"]'::jsonb, 'Umbilical vein to the inferior vena cava', 'The ductus venosus shunts oxygenated blood from the umbilical vein past the liver to the IVC.'),
